In-Reply-To: <BAA35444B19AD940997ED02A6996AAE001DE15BC@sanmail.picr.man.ac.uk>
References: <BAA35444B19AD940997ED02A6996AAE001DE15BC@sanmail.picr.man.ac.uk>
Message-ID: <1100626364.9955.4.camel@ybrig.MCB.McGill.CA>

Hi everyone,

we've been looking at something similar to try to pick single a series
of genes from the heatmap.

Based on Michael's suggestion:

d <- dist(mydata)
hc <- hclust(d)
heatmap(mydata, RowV=as.dendrogram(hc))

genes<-identify(hc)

So you can select the branch(es) of interest on the dendogram and get
back the list of genes selected.

Francois

