Hi,
read.maimages does not use information from the targets file in data uploading so it cannot know about the Cy3, Cy5 RNA labelling columns. If you look in the relevant code for read.maimage, the targets element in the RG list is written from the following line,

RG$targets <- data.frame(FileName = I(files), row.names = names)

These *are* only the filenames. If you want to update the targets element in the RG list then you could reassign the target informatino to the list element RG$targets.

RG <-read.maimages(files=targets$FileName, source="agilent", path="C:/caimiao/day1", 
